            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery aneurysm rupture mimicking dissection of the thoracic aorta.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>115-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute dissection of the ascending aorta may present with chest pain and haemopericardium. The following case illustrates an unusual differential diagnosis: rupture of a very large coronary artery aneurysm, diagnosed by transoesophageal echocardiography.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
